  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, be a fixed point in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>-plane. The image of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and the image of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, &nbsp;is a point in the fourth quadrant such that the maximum area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;square units, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to _____",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is the image of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;on y-axis</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is the image of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;in x-axis</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Area of triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mtd><mtd><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>a</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The maximum&nbsp;area of triangle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p>",
